he four moves from /etc/passwd to RCE, and which still work in 2026.",date:"2026-05-12",sources:[{name:"CWE-22: Improper Limitation of a Pathname to a Restricted Directory",url:"https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/22.html",publisher:"MITRE"},{name:"PHP manual: include and require",url:"https://www.php.net/manual/en/function.include.php",publisher:"PHP Group"},{name:"PHP manual: supported protocols and wrappers",url:"https://www.php.net/manual/en/wrappers.php",publisher:"PHP Group"},{name:"proc(5): the /proc filesystem",url:"https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man5/proc.5.html",publisher:"man7.org"},{name:"CVE-2021-41773: Apache HTTP Server path traversal",url:"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2021-41773",publisher:"NIST NVD"},{name:"Filesystem Hierarchy Standard 3.0",url:"https://refspecs.linuxfoundation.org/FHS_3.0/fhs/index.html",publisher:"Linux Foundation"}],tags:["web-exploitation","lfi","ctf-tools"]},{title:"Python Sandbox Bypass for CTF: The Filter-Breaker Playbook",seoTitle:"Python Sandbox Bypass for CTF (Pyjail)",slug:"python-sandbox-bypass-ctf",description:"Every Python pyjail filter can be broken. Learn string surgery, MRO traversal, breakpoint(), and namespace hijacking with picoCTF receipts.",date:"2026-05-14",sources:[{name:"Python data model: special attributes and the class hierarchy",url:"https://docs.python.org/3/reference/datamodel.html",publisher:"Python Software Foundation"},{name:"Python built-in functions: eval, exec, compile",url:"https://docs.python.org/3/library/functions.html",publisher:"Python Software Foundation"},{name:"Python audit hooks: sys.addaudithook",url:"https://docs.python.org/3/library/sys.html#sys.addaudithook",publisher:"Python Software Foundation"},{name:"PEP 578: Python Runtime Audit Hooks",url:"https://peps.python.org/pep-0578/",publisher:"Python Software Foundation"},{name:"CPython issue tracker: rexec and Bastion removal",url:"https://docs.python.org/2/library/rexec.html",publisher:"Python Software Foundation"}],tag