l computer security competition",url:"https://www.cmu.edu/news/stories/archives/2013/march/march13_computercontest.html",publisher:"Carnegie Mellon University"},{name:"Our Project (Toaster Wars)",url:"https://www.etc.cmu.edu/projects/osiris/?page_id=20",publisher:"Team Osiris, CMU Entertainment Technology Center"},{name:"PicoCTF Returns for Second Year",url:"https://www.cmu.edu/news/stories/archives/2014/october/october17_picocapturetheflag.html",publisher:"Carnegie Mellon University"},{name:"How to teach cybersecurity without scaring students away",url:"https://www.cylab.cmu.edu/news/2019/06/21-teach-cybersecurity-picoctf.html",publisher:"CMU CyLab Security and Privacy Institute"},{name:"picoCTF aims to close the cybersecurity talent gap",url:"https://www.cylab.cmu.edu/news/2025/07/14-picoctf.html",publisher:"CMU CyLab Security and Privacy Institute"},{name:"picoCTF returns in 2026 with more challenges and more prizes",url:"https://www.cylab.cmu.edu/news/2026/02/26-picoctf.html",publisher:"CMU CyLab Security and Privacy Institute"},{name:"CMU's picoCTF seeks to make cybersecurity education more accessible",url:"https://www.cmu.edu/news/stories/archives/2024/june/cmus-picoctf-seeks-to-make-cybersecurity-education-more-accessible",publisher:"Carnegie Mellon University"},{name:"picoCTF 2019 competition report",url:"https://www.cmu.edu/ini/news/2019/picoctf2019.html",publisher:"CMU Information Networking Institute"}],tags:["picoctf","beginner","guide","general-skills","ctf-history","learning-path"]},{title:"Race Conditions and TOCTOU for CTF: Winning the Window Between Check and Use",seoTitle:"Race Conditions and TOCTOU for CTF",slug:"race-conditions-toctou-ctf",description:"How to find, widen and win race conditions in CTF: symlink TOCTOU on SUID binaries, limit-overrun bugs in web apps, signal races, and mempool front-running.",date:"2026-08-15",sources:[{name:"CWE-367: Time-of-check Time-of-use (TOCTOU) Race Condition",url:"https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/367.html",publisher:"MITRE"},{name:"rename(2) manual page",url:"https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/rename.2.html",publisher:"Linux man-pages project"},{name:"open(2) manual page",url:"https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/open.2.html",publisher:"Linux man-pages project"},{name:"access(2) manual page",url:"https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/access.2.html",publisher:"Linux man-pages project"},{name:"Smashing the state machine: the true potential of web race conditions",url:"https://portswigger.net/research/smashing-the-state-machine",publisher:"PortSwigger Research"},{name:"RFC 9113: HTTP/2",url:"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9113.html",publisher:"IETF"},{name:"signal-safety(7) manual page",url:"https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man7/signal-safety.7.html",publisher:"Linux man-pages project"}],tags:["binary-exploitation","web-exploitation","race-conditions","linux","privilege-escalation","concurrency"]},{title:"PHP Type Juggling for CTF: Magic Hashes, Array Tricks, and What PHP 8 Broke",seoTitle:"PHP Type Juggling for CTF",slug:"php-type-juggling-ctf",description:"Loose comparison bugs in PHP, from 0e magic hashes to passing arrays into strcmp, plus which classic tricks PHP 8 killed and which ones still work in 2026.",date:"2026-08-17",sources:[{name:"PHP Manual: Comparison Operators",url:"https://www.php.net/manual/en/language.operators.comparison.php",publisher:"The PHP Group"},{name:"PHP Manual: Type Juggling",url:"https://www.php.net/manual/en/language.types.type-juggling.php",publisher:"The PHP Group"},{name:"PHP RFC: Saner string to number comparisons",url:"https://wiki.php.net/rfc/string_to_number_comparison",publisher:"The PHP Group"},{name:"PHP Manual: Backward Incompatible Changes in PHP 8.0",url:"https://www.php.net/manual/en/migration80.incompatible.php",publisher:"The PHP Group"},{name:"PHP RFC: Consistent type errors for internal functions",url:"https://wiki.php.net/rfc/consistent_type_errors",publisher:"The PHP Group"},{name:"PHP Manual: strcmp",ur